Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.1 Conditions to the Obligations of Acquirer. The obligations of Acquirer to consummate the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver at or prior to the Effective Time of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. (i) The representations and warranties of the Target set forth in Article IV shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date as though made on and as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that do not, individually or in the aggregate, constitute a Material Adverse Effect. Additionally, notwithstanding the foregoing, in the event that any such representation or warranty is qualified by materiality or a Material Adverse Effect, such qualification shall be disregarded for purposes of this Section 9.1(a)(i). (Page 102)
